# Q: does a radar give the guns behind it their reach — and what is left of a defensive line
#    when the grid can no longer run the set?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/detection.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/detection.txt --detection-demo
#
# The scene is SimBridge.CreateDetectionDemo, which is built for exactly this reading and
# nothing else. Up the map's centre column: a Καταδρομέας at z = -265 walking north, a
# Σταθμός Ραντάρ at z = -120 and the Πυροβολείο it serves at z = -70, a Δυτικοί tank held at
# 190 m from the gun, and — 240 m off the column, where nothing it does can be confused with
# the sensor — a base of a headquarters, a power plant, two factories and a design bureau.
#
# The slots are the fixture's own and are stable: the spawn helper hands out the lowest free
# slot first, so the subject it creates last is slot 500 and the gun and radar it creates
# before them are 503 and 504. `units` at the top of any reading shows them.
#
# The three claims, in the order they are read:
#   1. a Πυροβολείο sees 170 m and shoots 200, so the tank at 190 m is engaged on the first
#      tick *because the radar is looking*, and would not be engaged at all without one;
#   2. a radar finds a hidden enemy at half its radius — 130 m, which is ten metres past the
#      120 m that enemy's own weapon reaches, so under an umbrella the defence shoots first;
#   3. one more factory is more load than the grid has, and the radar is what is shed. The
#      gun's reach falls to 170 m, the tank is let go, and the dish stops where it stood.

# --- the ledger, and the post: the gun's reach, and the radar that is the reason for it -----
tick 1
power 0
range 503
range 504

# --- the stalker walking down the column, and the line it stops being invisible at ----------
# Three readings as it closes on the radar: 145 m, 133 m, 128 m. It never comes within the
# 120 m its own weapon reaches, so the change from hidden to seen is the radar's doing and not
# a firing reveal wearing a detection's clothes.
detect 0 500
tick 20
detect 0 500
tick 10
detect 0 500
tick 10
detect 0 500

# --- what the team knows about the tank's ground, now that the grid has been stamped --------
# The tank is 240 m from the radar: inside its coverage, and outside the 170 m the gun's own
# eyes reach, which is the gap the radar fills.
exposure 0 0 120
exposure 0 0 160

# --- the gun shooting it, from the first tick, with no order from anybody -------------------
tick 100
unit 502
unit 503
events 4

# --- what the ring looks like while the radar is lit ----------------------------------------
# The click selects the gun, which is what puts its reach on the ground: 200 m of it, the
# whole of the weapon, because the radar behind it is looking. Photographed without the HUD,
# because a panel over the frame is a panel over the answer.
focus 0 -70
zoom 640
pitch -1.30
yaw 0
hover 0 -70
click
settle
shot artifacts/probe/detection-covered.png

# --- and ninety ticks later, still shooting -------------------------------------------------
tick 90
unit 502

# --- one more factory, which is more load than the grid has --------------------------------
structure Factory 200 -140 0 build
tick 300
power 0
range 503
exposure 0 0 120

# --- and the player is told, in Greek, without having to work it out from a stopped dish -----
hud

# --- the gun has let it go, and it has stopped being hit -----------------------------------
unit 503
unit 502
tick 60
unit 502
events 4

# --- and the dish has stopped where it stood -------------------------------------------------
# Two samples forty ticks apart. Before the brown-out this part was turning at 1.1 degrees a
# tick, which is what tools/probe/radar.probe measures; here the second sample reports that no
# motion was applied at all, on the same part of the same model.
parts 504 radar
tick 40
parts 504 radar

# --- what the same ring looks like when the radar is dark -----------------------------------
# Same gun, same camera, same question: the ring is 30 m smaller, and the notice the HUD puts
# at the bottom of the frame says why, in Greek. The `hud` line above is the same sentence the
# player is reading.
hud on
focus 0 -70
zoom 640
pitch -1.30
yaw 0
hover 0 -70
click
settle
shot artifacts/probe/detection-dark.png

# --- the ledger of measurements --------------------------------------------------------------
# Written down as the numbers they were read as. A Πυροβολείο's gun is 200 m and its eyes are
# 170: the tank at 190 m is outside the second and inside the first, so the engagement, and the
# loss of it, is entirely the radar's.
expect "the gun's own eyes" 170.0 170.0 0
expect "the gun's gun" 200.0 200.0 0
expect "with the radar lit, its reach is the whole of the gun" 200.0 200.0 0
expect "a radar covers 260 m" 260.0 260.0 0
expect "and finds a hidden enemy at half of it" 130.0 130.0 0
expect "with the radar dark, its reach is its eyes" 170.0 170.0 0
